message: >-
  Cite the commit you read, by its hash and date; the citable work is the book
  described in preferred-citation. The manuscript is licensed under CC BY 4.0.
title: "Stochology: The Theory and Ethics of Aim under Uncertainty"
authors:
  - family-names: Neto
    given-names: Silvano
    email: dev@silvanoneto.com
repository: https://github.com/0b3st4f3r4/stochology
url: https://stochology.org
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Stochology is an integrative framework and transversal research program for the theory and
  ethics of aim (stókhos) for judgment and decision-making under structural uncertainty when
  action must precede the outcome. Its organizing object is the full mediation circuit across
  World, Archive, and Institution — an indivisibility inherited rather than discovered (Vickers
  1965 on regulation as the appreciation of a whole situation; Beer; Simon; the institutional
  economists). The argument is organized 1-to-1 around the Sequential Agent–World–Institution
  Loop, the Leontief Nuclear Triad M_Leontief = min(S_epi, S_vital, S_gov), the Three Canonical
  Operators, the Three Collapse Propositions, and the Seven Guard Sites (T1–T7: 3 direct
  transits, 3 reflexive locks, and 1 integral three-plane closure, 7 circuit transits in all).
  The treatise runs in five parts, 86 chapters (00–85) and five appendices; its architecture is
  the 35-layer Multilayer Knowledge Graph, 7 strata x 5 orders = C(7,3) = 35.
